# Scripts that run inside a Linux container must not be checked out with
# CRLF line endings (Task 30) — a CRLF shebang line breaks with
# "/bin/sh^M: bad interpreter". Scoped narrowly to the files that actually
# execute inside a container; not a repo-wide line-ending policy change.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Everything in the deploy package is read by shell on Linux (env example, compose files, docs the
# scripts quote). CRLF there broke env_value() and health.sh (drill finding F7).
deploy/** text eol=lf

# Repo-wide default: LF in the index and in working copies. The index is already all-LF,
# so this normalises nothing; it stops Windows checkouts producing CRLF noise.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.docx binary
*.mp4 binary
*.woff2 binary
